{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-984089","value":"17","numeric":17}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-984153","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"JM216","Cell_line":"L1210/S","Time(h)":48,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":1.2,"IC50_Dark_value":1.2,"Method":"Coulter cell counting","Notes":"Culture medium: RPMI 1640 with 10% horse serum; Cell density (cells/mL): 50000; Solvent: ethanol; Maximum solvent (%): 0.5","DOI":"10.1038/bjc.1994.320","Year":1994,"Type":"IC50"},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-984154","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"JM216","Cell_line":"L1210/cis","Time(h)":48,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":1.5,"IC50_Dark_value":1.5,"Method":"Coulter cell counting","Notes":"Culture medium: RPMI 1640 with 10% horse serum; Cell density (cells/mL): 50000; Solvent: ethanol; Maximum solvent (%): 0.5","DOI":"10.1038/bjc.1994.320","Year":1994,"Type":"IC50"},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-984155","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"JM216","Cell_line":"L1210/tetra","Time(h)":48,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":1.4,"IC50_Dark_value":1.4,"Method":"Coulter cell counting","Notes":"Culture medium: RPMI 1640 with 10% horse serum; Cell density (cells/mL): 50000; Solvent: ethanol; Maximum solvent (%): 0.5","DOI":"10.1038/bjc.1994.320","Year":1994,"Type":"IC50"},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-984156","Abbreviation_in_the_article":"JM216","Cell_line":"L1210/carbo","Time(h)":48,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":1.6,"IC50_Dark_value":1.6,"Method":"Coulter cell counting","Notes":"Culture medium: RPMI 1640 with 10% horse serum; Cell density (cells/mL): 50000; Solvent: ethanol; Maximum solvent (%): 0.5","DOI":"10.1038/bjc.1994.320","Year":1994,"Type":"IC50"}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"Satraplatin","value":-0.12,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","temperature_C":37,"doi":"10.1002/aoc.70416","year":2025,"record_id":"MLDB-001596","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The determination of the partition coefficients of target complexes using the classic n-octanol/water shake-flask method can be summarized as follows: First, equal volumes of n-octanol and purified water were mixed and shaken at 37°C for 24 h to allow mutual saturation of the two phases. After standing for 1 h, the phases were separated for later use. The complexes were dissolved in water-saturated n-octanol to prepare solutions at concentrations of 40, 60, 80, 100, and 120 μM. The absorbance of each concentration was measured in triplicate using a UV–Vis spectrophotometer, and the average values were used to construct a standard curve to ensure reliable linearity. Subsequently, n-octanol-saturated aqueous solution was placed in a centrifuge tube, and the target complex was added to prepare a 50 μM test sample. The mixture was shaken at 37°C for 48 h to ensure equilibrium distribution. After standing for 1 h, the phases were completely separated by centrifugation at 2500 rpm for 15 min. The solutions from both phases were sampled using syringes, and their absorbance values were measured in triplicate using a UV–Vis spectrophotometer. The average values were used for subsequent concentration calculations. The lipid phase concentration (Co) was calculated based on the standard curve, and the aqueous phase concentration (Cw) was determined using the principle of mass conservation. The LogPo/w of the complex was calculated using Equation (1): log Po/w = log(Co / Cw)"},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"Satraplatin","value":0.23,"value_relation":"=","std":0.01,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","doi":"10.1007/s00775-014-1214-6","year":2014,"record_id":"MLDB-001990","detection":"ICP-MS","method_description":"Lipophilicity was determined as the partition coefficient between n-octanol and water (log P o/w) and as the chromatographic retention factor (log k w). The log P o/w determination was carried out according to the OECD guidelines for the classical shake flask method [23] with slight modifications. The complexes were dissolved in Milli-Q water (pre-saturated with 1-octanol) and the platinum concentration was determined by ICP-MS. The remaining stock solution was mixed with an equal volume of 1-octanol (pre-saturated with Milli-Q water) and shaken for 1 h. After phase separation, the platinum concentration was again determined in the aqueous phase by ICP-MS and the partition coefficients were calculated assuming the missing quantity (compared to the stock solution) in the organic phase. ICP-MS measurements were carried out after dilution of the samples with 1 % HNO3 using the instrumental parameters given in Table 1."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"JM216","value":0.1,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","doi":"10.1021/jm9904250","year":2000,"record_id":"MLDB-002015"},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"JM216","value":-0.16,"value_relation":"=","std":0.16,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"0.9% NaCl","doi":"10.1054/bjoc.1999.1026","year":2000,"record_id":"MLDB-002178","detection":"ICP-MS","method_description":"The hydrophobicity (log P) of the series of compounds was determined using a shake-flask method (Albert, 1979). Aqueous (0.9% (w/v) sodium chloride (NaCl) and organic (n-octanol) phases were saturated for 1 week. Drugs were dissolved at a final concentration of 300 µM in the aqueous phase. An equal volume of saturated noctanol was added and the solutions mixed for 30 min (45 rpm). Samples were centrifuged (1500 g, 10 min) and the platinum content of the organic and aqueous phases determined by ICP-MS. The log of the ratio of platinum concentrations in the organic and aqueous phases were calculated to determine log P."},{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"Satraplatin","value":-0.11,"value_relation":"=","std":0.02,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","doi":"10.1016/j.jinorgbio.2024.112515","year":2024,"record_id":"MLDB-002231","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The equal volume of octanol and purified water were mixed and shaken in a shaker for 24 h for pre-saturated solution treatment. The equal volume pre-treated n-octanol and aqueous solution were precisely measured and mixed, and the tested complex was slowly added to the solution until saturated, then shaken in a shaker for 48 h, and centrifuged at 2500 r/min for 15 min. The absorbance of the two-phase solution was measured by UV–Vis, and log Pow was calculated by formula (4-1). Ao was the UV absorbance value of the complex in the lipid phase (n-octanol) at a specific wavelength, and Aw was the UV absorbance value of the complex in the water phase at the corresponding wavelength. logPow = log(Ao/Aw)"}]}